---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Training — Built Not Obsessed"
  description="The 80/20 training philosophy. Four days a week, compound movements, progressive overload — everything you need and nothing you don't."
>
  <Nav />

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="page-hero-bg"></div>
    <div class="page-hero-content">
      <div class="eyebrow">Training</div>
      <h1 class="page-headline">
        Four days.<br/>
        <span class="italic">All you need.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="page-sub">The gym should make your life better — not become your life. Here's how to build a body worth having without sacrificing everything else.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="philosophy-section">
    <div class="section-label">The Training Philosophy</div>
    <div class="philosophy-layout">
      <div class="philosophy-left">
        <h2 class="philosophy-headline">Less is more.<br/><span class="italic">We mean it.</span></h2>
        <p class="philosophy-text">Most gym culture is built on more — more days, more volume, more supplements, more sacrifice. We built this around a different question: what is the minimum effective dose to look great, feel strong, and still have a full life outside the gym?</p>
        <p class="philosophy-text">The answer is four days a week of focused, progressive training. Not five. Not six. Four — done with intention.</p>
        <div class="philosophy-stat-row">
          <div class="pstat">
            <div class="pstat-num">4</div>
            <div class="pstat-label">days per week</div>
          </div>
          <div class="pstat">
            <div class="pstat-num">60</div>
            <div class="pstat-label">minutes per session</div>
          </div>
          <div class="pstat">
            <div class="pstat-num">3</div>
            <div class="pstat-label">days to recover & live</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="philosophy-right">
        <div class="pullquote">
          <p>"The best program is the one you can sustain for years — not the one that destroys you in weeks."</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="principles-section">
    <div class="section-label">Core Principles</div>
    <div class="principles-grid">

      <div class="principle-card">
        <div class="principle-num">01</div>
        <h3 class="principle-title">Compound movements first</h3>
        <p class="principle-text">Squat, deadlift, bench press, overhead press, row. These five movement patterns build more muscle, burn more calories, and improve more athletic qualities than any machine or isolation exercise. Build your sessions around them and fill the rest in after.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="principle-card">
        <div class="principle-num">02</div>
        <h3 class="principle-title">Progressive overload is the only rule</h3>
        <p class="principle-text">Your body adapts to stress. If you lift the same weight for the same reps every week, nothing changes. The goal is simple: do a little more than last time. More weight, more reps, or better form. That's it. That's the whole game.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="principle-card">
        <div class="principle-num">03</div>
        <h3 class="principle-title">Recovery is part of training</h3>
        <p class="principle-text">Muscle isn't built in the gym — it's built when you rest. Sleep, nutrition, and stress management aren't optional extras. They're where the results actually happen. Three days off isn't laziness. It's the plan working.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="principle-card">
        <div class="principle-num">04</div>
        <h3 class="principle-title">Consistency beats intensity</h3>
        <p class="principle-text">Showing up four days a week for two years beats training twice a day for three months and burning out. The person who wins is the one still in the gym five years from now — not the one who went hardest in January.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="principle-card">
        <div class="principle-num">05</div>
        <h3 class="principle-title">The weekend is not the enemy</h3>
        <p class="principle-text">A night out, a few drinks, a big meal — none of these undo a week of good training. The math simply doesn't work that way. What kills progress is the guilt spiral that follows, not the night itself. Enjoy it and get back on track Monday.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="principle-card">
        <div class="principle-num">06</div>
        <h3 class="principle-title">Train for the long game</h3>
        <p class="principle-text">The goal isn't to look good for a vacation. The goal is to be strong, capable, and healthy at 40, 50, and 60. That means training smart — protecting your joints, managing fatigue, and building habits that compound over decades, not crash diets that expire in weeks.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="structure-section">
    <div class="section-label">The Weekly Structure</div>
    <div class="week-layout">
      <div class="week-intro">
        <h2 class="week-headline">How the week is built</h2>
        <p class="week-text">The 4-day structure follows an upper/lower split — one of the most well-researched and time-tested approaches in strength training. Each muscle group gets trained twice a week with enough recovery between sessions to actually grow.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="week-grid">
        <div class="day-card active">
          <div class="day-label">Monday</div>
          <div class="day-title">Upper — Strength</div>
          <p class="day-text">Heavy compound pressing and pulling. Low reps, high effort. This is where you build raw strength.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="day-card rest">
          <div class="day-label">Tuesday</div>
          <div class="day-title">Rest / Walk</div>
          <p class="day-text">Active recovery. A walk, a stretch, or nothing at all. Your body is working even when you're not lifting.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="day-card active">
          <div class="day-label">Wednesday</div>
          <div class="day-title">Lower — Strength</div>
          <p class="day-text">Squats, deadlifts, and posterior chain work. The foundation of everything. Don't skip leg day.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="day-card rest">
          <div class="day-label">Thursday</div>
          <div class="day-title">Rest / Walk</div>
          <p class="day-text">Another recovery day. Use it. Go outside. Eat well. Sleep. This is training too.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="day-card active">
          <div class="day-label">Friday</div>
          <div class="day-title">Upper — Hypertrophy</div>
          <p class="day-text">Moderate weight, higher reps. More volume, more muscle stimulus. This is where size is built.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="day-card rest">
          <div class="day-label">Saturday</div>
          <div class="day-title">Live Your Life</div>
          <p class="day-text">Go out. Have dinner. Drink a beer. This is not a cheat day — it's the whole point.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="day-card active">
          <div class="day-label">Sunday</div>
          <div class="day-title">Lower — Hypertrophy</div>
          <p class="day-text">Volume work for legs and glutes. Finish the week strong. Then rest until Monday.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="day-card">
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="cta-strip">
    <div class="cta-text">
      <span class="cta-sub">Ready to start</span>
      Simple. Sustainable. Effective.
    </div>
    <a href="mailto:hello@builtnotobsessed.com" class="btn-dark">Get the Full Program</a>
  </div>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  :root {
    --ink: #0f0e0d;
    --cream: #f5f0e8;
    --warm: #e8dcc8;
    --amber: #c8832a;
    --amber-light: #e8a840;
    --rust: #9e3b1f;
    --muted: #7a7268;
  }

  .page-hero {
    min-height: 60vh;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    padding: 0 2.5rem 5rem;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--ink);
    padding-top: 80px;
  }

  .page-hero-bg {
    position: absolute; inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(15,14,13,0.4) 0%, rgba(15,14,13,0.95) 100%);
  }

  .page-hero-content { position: relative; max-width: 800px; }

  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.65rem; letter-spacing: 0.3em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--amber); font-weight: 500;
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .eyebrow::before {
    content: ''; display: block; width: 40px; height: 1px; background: var(--amber);
  }

  .page-headline {
    font-family: 'Bebas Neue', Impact, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(56px, 9vw, 120px);
    line-height: 0.92; letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    color: var(--cream); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .italic {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif;
    font-style: italic; font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--warm);
  }

  .page-sub {
    font-size: 1rem; color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 520px; line-height: 1.7;
    font-weight: 300;
  }

  .section-label {
    font-size: 0.65rem; letter-spacing: 0.25em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--amber); font-weight: 500;
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .section-label::after {
    content: ''; flex: 1; max-width: 60px; height: 1px;
    background: var(--amber); opacity: 0.5;
  }

  .philosophy-section {
    padding: 6rem 2.5rem;
    background: var(--ink);
  }

  .philosophy-layout {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 5rem; align-items: center;
  }

  .philosophy-headline {
    font-family: 'Bebas Neue', Impact, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(42px, 5vw, 72px);
    line-height: 1; color: var(--cream);
    margin-bottom: 2rem; letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }

  .philosophy-text {
    font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.8; font-weight: 300;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .philosophy-stat-row {
    display: flex; gap: 2.5rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(200,131,42,0.2);
  }

  .pstat-num {
    font-family: 'Bebas Neue', Impact, sans-serif;
    font-size: 3rem; color: var(--amber); line-height: 1;
  }

  .pstat-label {
    font-size: 0.7rem; color: var(--muted);
    text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }

  .pullquote {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--amber);
    padding: 2.5rem 3rem;
    background: rgba(200,131,42,0.05);
  }

  .pullquote p {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.5vw, 1.8rem);
    font-style: italic; font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--cream); line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .principles-section {
    padding: 6rem 2.5rem;
    background: rgba(200,131,42,0.03);
  }

  .principles-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0; border: 1px solid rgba(200,131,42,0.2);
  }

  .principle-card {
    padding: 3rem 2.5rem;
    border-right: 1px solid rgba(200,131,42,0.2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(200,131,42,0.2);
    position: relative; overflow: hidden;
    transition: background 0.3s;
  }

  .principle-card:nth-child(even) { border-right: none; }
  .principle-card:nth-child(5),
  .principle-card:nth-child(6) { border-bottom: none; }
  .principle-card:hover { background: rgba(200,131,42,0.04); }

  .principle-num {
    font-family: 'Bebas Neue', Impact, sans-serif;
    font-size: 4.5rem; color: rgba(200,131,42,0.1);
    position: absolute; top: 1rem; right: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1; user-select: none;
  }

  .principle-title {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--cream); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .principle-text {
    font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.75; font-weight: 300;
  }

  .structure-section {
    padding: 6rem 2.5rem;
    background: var(--ink);
  }

  .week-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr; gap: 5rem; align-items: start; }

  .week-headline {
    font-family: 'Bebas Neue', Impact, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(36px, 4vw, 56px);
    color: var(--cream); line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem; letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }

  .week-text {
    font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.8; font-weight: 300;
  }

  .week-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1px; background: rgba(200,131,42,0.15);
  }

  .day-card {
    background: var(--ink);
    padding: 1.75rem 2rem;
    transition: background 0.2s;
  }

  .day-card:hover { background: rgba(200,131,42,0.05); }

  .day-card.active { border-left: 2px solid var(--amber); }
  .day-card.rest { border-left: 2px solid rgba(200,131,42,0.2); }

  .day-label {
    font-size: 0.6rem; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted); font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .day-card.active .day-label { color: var(--amber); }

  .day-title {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--cream); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .day-text {
    font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.6; font-weight: 300;
  }

  .cta-strip {
    background: var(--amber); padding: 4rem 2.5rem;
    display: flex; align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between; gap: 2rem; flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .cta-text {
    font-family: 'Bebas Neue', Impact, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    color: var(--ink); line-height: 1;
  }

  .cta-sub {
    display: block;
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 0.3em; font-weight: 400;
    font-style: italic; opacity: 0.7;
  }

  .btn-dark {
    background: var(--ink); color: var(--amber);
    padding: 1rem 2.5rem; border-radius: 2px;
    font-size: 0.75rem; letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    font-weight: 500; text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none; transition: opacity 0.2s; flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .btn-dark:hover { opacity: 0.85; }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .philosophy-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 3rem; }
    .principles-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .principle-card:nth-child(even) { border-right: 1px solid rgba(200,131,42,0.2); }
    .principle-card:nth-child(5) { border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(200,131,42,0.2); }
    .principle-card:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
    .week-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 3rem; }
    .week-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
